<title>FRANCE: French tobacco duty to rise 4.8 bln francs.</title>
<headline>French tobacco duty to rise 4.8 bln francs.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said that an increase in tobacco duties would raise 4.8 billion francs and that an increase in alcohol duties would raise 1.8 billion francs.</p>
<p>Petrol duties would rise six centimes per litre, he added.</p>
<p>Arthuis told a 1997 budget news conference that three billion francs of the extra tobacco duty revenues would go directly to fund the welfare system.</p>
</text>
